### Signing in at a provider.

## Why a sign-in by code was refused here or by the site.

oauth-unusable-id = the application id is not one that can be sent
# Put after what GitLab said when it refused to give a code; "Device authorization grant" is what GitLab calls the setting.
oauth-device-grant-off = (the application may not sign in by code: turn on its "Device authorization grant" at the site)
oauth-only-gitlab-renews = only GitLab's tokens are renewed

## What of the site's answer was not as it should be.

oauth-not-json = not JSON
oauth-device-code = the device code
oauth-user-code = the user code
oauth-verification = the address to type the code at
oauth-verification-elsewhere = the address to type the code at is not on the site
oauth-no-token = no token in the answer
